  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two integers NNN and MMM.\n\nLet pr(x)\\text{pr}(x)pr(x) denote the number of distinct **prime** factors of xxx.\n\nCount the number of integer arrays AAA such that:\n\n\nAAA has length NNN.\n1≤Ai≤M1 \\leq A_i \\leq M1≤Ai​≤M, and all the elements of AAA are **distinct**.\npr(Ai)≤pr(Aj)\\text{pr}(A_i) \\leq \\text{pr}(A_j)pr(Ai​)≤pr(Aj​) for 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq N1≤i&lt;j≤N.\nThe number of such arrays can be large, so print the answer modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and the only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers - NNN and MMM.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of arrays satisfying the conditions, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤M≤1051 \\leq N \\leq M \\leq 10^51≤N≤M≤105",
      "The sum of MMM across all test cases doesn't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 3\n2 4\n100 100",
        "output": "4\n9\n826359883",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The four possible arrays are:\n[1,2],[1,3],[2,3],[3,2][1, 2], [1, 3], [2, 3], [3, 2][1,2],[1,3],[2,3],[3,2].\nTest case 222: The nine possible arrays are:\n[1,2],[1,3],[1,4][1, 2], [1, 3], [1, 4][1,2],[1,3],[1,4]\n[2,3],[2,4][2, 3], [2, 4][2,3],[2,4]\n[3,2],[3,4][3, 2], [3, 4][3,2],[3,4]\n[4,2],[4,4][4, 2], [4, 4][4,2],[4,4]\nNote that pr(2)=pr(3)=pr(4)=1\\text{pr}(2) = \\text{pr}(3) = \\text{pr}(4) = 1pr(2)=pr(3)=pr(4)=1."
      }
    ]
  },
